It is not unusual to employ separate models for the first few observations
in a time series, e.g.

  p(y) = p(y[1])
         * p(y[2] | y[1])
         * p(y[3] | y[1:2])
         * PROD_{n > 3} p(y[n] | y[n-3:n-1]) ...

You just need to formulate models for the first three terms.

- Bob

